<p>The US Justice Department said it will again allow firing squads, electrocution, and gas asphyxiation in federal death penalty cases, while also restoring the lethal injection protocol used during President Trump&#x27;s first term. The department also said it will streamline internal processes to speed death penalty cases after appeals are exhausted, casting the policy as part of the Trump administration&#x27;s broader push to pursue capital punishment more aggressively in federal cases. The change reverses Biden-era limits on federal executions. Before leaving office in January 2025, Joe Biden commuted 37 of 40 federal death row sentences to life without parole, leaving three federal inmates still facing execution. The move lands as capital punishment remains deeply debated in the United States, with critics continuing to warn about fairness and the risk of wrongful convictions.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/rHZ8beC5BqRmEnC5O3dYhXO_aHTRTzGOZHKM7pkTHkZpFZ-nuxELYuCeGu8VZaXnUP1bLYyKLorLNuoDTKRq62pZupvzjZO77UkZPp4gU2Qo' alt='The death chamber and the steel bars of the viewing room are seen at the federal penitentiary in Huntsville, Texas September 29, 2010.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Execution pace: The federal government carried out 13 executions by lethal injection during the final six months of President Trump&#x27;s first term, more than under any US president in 120 years.</li></ul><blockquote>The prior administration failed in its duty to protect the American people by refusing to pursue and carry out the ultimate punishment against the most dangerous criminals, including terrorists, child murderers, and cop killers. - Acting Attorney General Todd Blanche</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>US Justice Department: The department said the revised policy will make the death penalty a stronger deterrent and speed up cases by simplifying internal procedures once appeals end. (<a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cg73l2d079ko'>BBC</a>)</li><li>Trump administration: At the start of his second term, President Trump called on the Justice Department to expand the use of capital punishment for what he described as the vilest crimes. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1994896/trump-seeks-to-bring-back-firing-squads-for-executions'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Critics of capital punishment: Opponents cited by Al Jazeera warn that prioritizing executions raises the risk of irreversible miscarriages of justice because innocent people can be sentenced to death. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/4/24/trump-administration-to-prioritize-seeking-death-penalty-use-firing-squads'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/news/639041-us-executions-firing-electrocution-gas/'>US to bring back gas chambers, electric chairs and firing squads for federal executions</a> - rt.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1994896/trump-seeks-to-bring-back-firing-squads-for-executions'>Trump seeks to bring back  firing squads  for executions</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/4/24/trump-administration-to-prioritize-seeking-death-penalty-use-firing-squads'>Trump administration to prioritise seeking death penalty, use firing squads</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cg73l2d079ko'>US to allow firing squads, gas, and electrocution for federal executions</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/united-states-canada/article/3351388/trump-justice-department-adds-firing-squads-federal-executions'>Trump Justice Department adds firing squads for federal executions</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/us-justice-department-allows-use-of-firing-squads-for-federal-executions-11405896#publisher=newsstand'>US Justice Department Allows Use Of Firing Squads For Federal Executions</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/united-states/justice-department-readop